---
description: "JS/TS frontend conventions"
globs:
  - "**/*.ts"
  - "**/*.tsx"
  - "**/*.js"
  - "**/*.jsx"
alwaysApply: false
---

Frontend conventions for this project.

- TypeScript strict mode; no `any` without a written justification.
- Prefer function components and hooks; avoid class components.
- Server state goes through your data-fetching layer (TanStack Query, RTK
  Query, SWR, etc.); do not fetch directly inside components.
- Use the design-system primitives (shadcn, MUI, Chakra, etc.) instead of
  inline styles; keep styling in the configured system (Tailwind classes,
  CSS modules, etc.).
- Generated API client code is read-only; regenerate from the contract
  (OpenAPI/GraphQL) instead of hand-editing.
- Never log auth tokens, session cookies, or PII to the browser console in
  production builds.
